WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935
-Well, for those of you keeping
track at home,

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:04.471
the president's friends are
Vladimir Putin and Kim Jong-Un,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his enemies are Playboy
bunnies and Joe Biden.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.076 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.710 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Did you hear about this?

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.514
First Joe Biden said that he
would have beaten up Trump

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in high school.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then Trump tweeted that he'd
beat Biden in a fight

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Biden would go down
fast and hard.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:24.457
And women everywhere said
thank God we didn't elect

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
an emotional woman
to lead our country.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now we have this to deal with.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's right.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even though they're both
in their 70s,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
Biden and Trump
are talking about fighting.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.439 size:78% position:39%
Experts say the match
would go nine rounds

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
with 10 bathroom breaks.
-Ho!

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.078 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:45.578 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's crazy.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.680
Biden and Trump are threatening
to beat each other up.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
It got even weirder
when Bernie Sanders

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:52.652
ripped off his shirt and yelled,
"Tag me in, let's do this thing!

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come at me, bro!"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Come at me, bro.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.193
Straight after Biden brought up
the idea of fighting Trump,

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
the president sent this tweet,
and this is real.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:06.499
He said, "Crazy Joe Biden is
trying to act like a tough guy.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.167 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He doesn't know me,

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he would go down fast
and hard, crying all the way."

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Wow.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:12.806 line:92%
Then Biden actually replied.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "White House,
bike racks, 3:00, be there!"

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:20.480 line:92%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.948 line:92%
Then Trump said, "Uh, I can't.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told my dad
I'd wash the car at 3:00."

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.921
Then Biden said, "No way, you
can't back out! No backsies!"

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Trump said,
"No backsies, infinity!"

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.893 line:92%
Hopefully they can work it out.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.494 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Some tech news.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that
since Facebook's data breach,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of users
have deleted their accounts.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.367
Which is tough, because now they
come over to your house

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.636 size:84% position:42%
to show you pictures of
their kids in person.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're like, "Yeah, that's
great. Like, like, like."

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.241 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.742 line:92%
Last night Mark Zuckerberg said

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's focused on
rebuilding trust.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.546 size:88% position:44%
Facebook users said that
lying is unacceptable.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.417
Then went back to RSVP'ing "yes"
to events they'll never go to.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.219 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's like, uh, maybe?

00:01:59.219 --> 00:01:59.819 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Listen to this.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:04.791
Marvel is calling the upcoming
film, "Avengers: Infinity War"

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
the most ambitious
crossover ever.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.697
Though, I'm pretty sure the most
ambitious crossover ever

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
is actually President Trump's
hair.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it starts here,
and it's like --

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.503 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told you, I think he uses
a Dyson Airblade.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Does he really?
-Yeah.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:27.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.148 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I saw that Toys "R" Us

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
is having a giant
"going out of business" sale.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:31.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can either go to the
store today and pay half price

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
or pay nothing at the Dumpster
behind the store tomorrow.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.358 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's up to you.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.993 size:75% position:38%
You make your plans.
I don't make plans.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard about a man in Arizona
who called the police,

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:45.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
asking if the dinosaur
decorations in his local park

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.768 size:75% position:38% line:92%
were real dinosaurs.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The cops said no,

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.272
but the mushrooms you ate
were definitely real, so...

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sit down, maybe.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally, you guys,
Easter is coming up,

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:01.314
and a lot of people are getting
ready for the big holiday.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.582 line:92%
So we went down to the NBC Plaza

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
to ask people
about their Easter plans.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:05.685 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The only catch is,

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.820
they all had to answer
with a mouthful of Peeps.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.557
I'll show you what I mean
in another installment of

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Where My Peeps At?"
Here we go.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:18.364 line:92%
♪♪ -Where my Peeps at, ooh ♪♪

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.766 line:92%
-What are your plans for Easter?

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.834 line:92%
-I'm going to my mother's.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
My mother's house.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.040 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:35.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.849 line:92%
-What was that last part?

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.222 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.290 line:92%
-Do you really want to know?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.826 line:92%
I have to get a colonoscopy.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Eat Peeps.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Eat Peeps.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.602 line:92%
-We've got a great show tonight!

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for the Roots,
everybody!

